 # Atomic warehouse adjustments
 
-Existing action snapshot is exposed through api.dispatch and python cli.py, accepting one JSON object on stdin and writing one JSON result.
+Actions are routed through `api.dispatch(payload)` and `python cli.py`, which accepts one JSON object on stdin and writes one JSON result on stdout.
+
+## Actions
+
+### snapshot
+
+`{"action": "snapshot", "db": "/abs/path/stock.db"}` — returns all stock rows as `[{"sku": ..., "quantity": ...}, ...]` sorted by sku using Python string order.
+
+### adjust
+
+`{"action": "adjust", "db": "/abs/path/stock.db", "changes": [{"sku": "A", "delta": -5}, ...]}` — applies up to 100 changes (each delta an integer in -1000..1000) to the `stock(sku TEXT PRIMARY KEY, quantity INTEGER NOT NULL)` table in one atomic transaction, in input order. Repeated SKUs are allowed; each delta applies to the latest quantity. On success the new quantities are persisted and all rows are returned sorted by sku (Python string order). An empty `changes` list returns the current rows unchanged.
+
+Concrete invocation:
+
+    echo '{"action": "adjust", "db": "/abs/path/stock.db", "changes": [{"sku": "A", "delta": -5}, {"sku": "B", "delta": 3}]}' | python cli.py
+
+## Boundary and error semantics
+
+- A delta that takes a quantity to exactly 0 is valid; quantities may not go below zero.
+- A missing SKU or an intermediate quantity below zero raises `ValueError` and rolls back every change from that call, leaving the database untouched.
+- Unknown actions raise `ValueError`. The CLI exits 2 with a nonempty stderr message and no traceback on `ValueError`; successful calls exit 0 with JSON on stdout.
+- Only the named database file is modified; no new rows and no schema changes are ever made.
